# Runtime Topology SSOT

RULE: Runtime messaging/storage/API interaction policy must live in `unified-trading-deployment-v3/configs/runtime-topology.yaml`. Code dependency DAG must live in `unified-trading-pm/workspace-manifest.json`. Do not hardcode runtime transport behavior in service repos or create service-to-service dependencies for live paths.
WHY: DAG boundaries stay clean only when runtime deployment topology is declarative and owned by deployment config.
CODEX: 00-SSOT-INDEX.md, 04-architecture/TOPOLOGY-DAG.md, 04-architecture/batch-live-symmetry.md

DO:
- Use exactly two machine-readable SSOTs: `workspace-manifest.json` (code DAG) + `runtime-topology.yaml` (runtime interactions)
- Treat `dependencies.yaml` as derived readiness-check data, not a primary SSOT
- Configure per-edge mode behavior (`batch` vs `live`) via `transport` and `deployment_profile`
- Use `in_memory` only when `deployment_profile=co_located_vm`
- Keep services thin: they select mode/adapters, not infrastructure discovery logic

NEVER:
- Add service-to-service import or pyproject dependency to enable live in-memory handoff
- Encode co-location assumptions directly in service code
- Use runtime topology docs that diverge from `runtime-topology.yaml`
